      <div type="clause" n="7.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IudDeiXIV">Iud Dei XIV</ref> 7.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Iud Dei XIV 7.2" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="426" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis uero pertinax ausu temerario maculatus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IudDeiXIV_7-2.lnote.oe.23"/> de his quae hic tenentur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IudDeiXIV_7-2.lnote.oe.24"/> inserta, ore sacrilego te edere conatus fuerit, fauces uel guttur illius transire non possis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#IudDeiXIV_7-2.lnote.oe.25"/>; sed strangulatus sentiat, Deum, quem nulla latent, in sua creatura miracula operari, ut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#IudDeiXIV_7-2.lnote.oe.26"/> confusus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#IudDeiXIV_7-2.lnote.oe.27"/> proferat et reiciat quod sponte nolebat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#IudDeiXIV_7-2.lnote.oe.28"/>, detque gloriam Deo, qui uenturus est<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#IudDeiXIV_7-2.lnote.oe.29"/> iudicare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#IudDeiXIV_7-2.lnote.oe.30"/>.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann"/>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">2 Tim. 4, 1</note>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 426 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
